+# Accessibility remediation integration
+
+## Components and ownership
+
+Conductor authenticates the instructor and checks project edit permission before resolving the source page from the stored project section. It proxies page actions through the Remedy gateway, which forwards to the Remedy bridge. The bridge generates reviewed changes and performs guarded CXone writes. Credentials remain server-managed; instructor-owned inference keys are not supported.
+
+- Conductor: `server/api/remediationqueue.ts`, `server/api/remediationactions.ts`, `client/src/components/projects/RemediationWorkQueue.tsx`, and `RemediationPageActions.tsx`.
+- Remedy gateway: `backend/app/cxone_routes.py` in `libretexts-remedy-server-dev`.
+- Remedy bridge: `packages/conductor-panel/server/server.ts` and `packages/core/src/{review-alt,revert,agent-loop}.ts` in `libretexts-remedy-bridge-dev`.
+
+## Workflow and API
+
+The queue is mounted on the project accessibility page. A task opens its source page; a fresh scan selects the finding by rule and selector. The reviewer generates a preview, inspects the image and diff, optionally edits proposed alt text, acknowledges the reviewed preview, and applies it. Apply rescans the source and attaches evidence to the originating task. Restore lists saved versions, requires a separate preview and acknowledgement, then restores and rescans.
+
+Conductor routes use `/project/:projectID/accessibility/workqueue`. Page actions use `/page/:sectionID/:action` beneath that base: `scan`, `preview`, `revise-preview`, `apply`, `snapshots`, `restore-preview`, and `restore`. Browser-supplied source page IDs, URLs, snapshot paths, and scan evidence are not authoritative.
+
+Queue records persist in MongoDB with a unique project/finding key, optimistic version checks, assignment, priority, history, and scan evidence. Verification requires a reviewer note. Neither apply, scan, nor restore automatically verifies a task.
+
+## Configuration and safeguards
+
+Conductor uses `REMEDY_API_BASE_URL` and the existing gateway authentication configuration. Deploy the gateway recovery routes and bridge endpoints together with the Conductor changes. Preserve each deployment's environment files, compose overrides, networks, and persistent snapshot volume.
+
+Bridge inference settings are documented in its `.env.example`. The shared client supports Ollama primary and OpenAI fallback for text, vision, and advanced agent tool calls. OpenAI tool calls use Responses, with tool-result and reasoning-context replay. Availability failures can trigger fallback; invalid requests and refusals do not.
+
+Static GIF and other supported static image formats are decoded to PNG for inference. Animated/multipage images require manual review. Conversion does not replace the original source image. Reviewed alt edits are restricted to images in the selected preview, escape attribute content, and preserve surrounding HTML.
+
+Apply and restore validate the live content hash. Restore binds its expiring token to the page and snapshot, validates snapshot metadata and content integrity, and creates a safety snapshot before writing. CXone writes retain the existing sandbox guard. A successful content write followed by a scan/evidence failure is reported separately so the reviewer can retry the scan without repeating the write.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Remedy core: `npm run test --workspace @libretexts/remedy-core -- --run` — 155 tests passed.
+- Conductor, from `server`: `./node_modules/.bin/tsx --test util/remediationactions.test.ts util/remediationqueue.test.ts util/corsPolicy.test.ts util/a11yreviewutils.test.ts` — 15 tests passed.
+- Gateway: `python3 -m pytest tests/unit/test_cxone_recovery_routes.py -q` — 2 tests passed.
+- Focused TypeScript checks cover the new client/server modules and bridge core.
+
+Browser acceptance on 2026-09-13 covered task creation, source-image inference, edited preview, single-attribute apply, rescan, restore, evidence persistence, assignment, filtering, duplicate prevention, and required verification evidence. On a sandbox page, total findings changed 14 → 13 → 14 and the target criterion changed fail → pass → fail. The restore preview matched the original full-page HTML, and the final rescan confirmed the original finding returned. The content change was intentionally restored.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- The deployed legacy matrix requires its reload control to display newly saved scan results; the task panel and evidence update immediately.
+- Page tools currently uses scan-success wording that claims task evidence was attached even when no task was selected.
+- A short alt summary does not expose every value in an image of a data table. Such images still need an accessible table or longer description and human review, even if the automatic alt check passes.
+- Model output requires subject-matter review. Automated checks are not accessibility certification.
+- The full legacy application build and every page-wide agent strategy are outside this scoped acceptance run.
+
+## Deployment notes
+
+The isolated `client/src/remediation-queue-entry.tsx` supports layering the same UI onto an existing compiled application. Normal source builds mount the component through `ProjectAccessibility.jsx`. The integration source is the durable handoff; environment-specific image tags and deployment credentials are managed separately.
